 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No hands on «واستغفروا ربكم»; light for «إن ربي رحيم ودود», geometric for «إن ربي بما تعملون محيط», an hourglass for «سوف تعلمون». Their scorn of Shu'ayb (91:8-11, 15-18) is not glossed; 91:1-7 carries As-Sa'di's reason «لبغضهم لما يقول». 93:1-4 «اعملوا على مكانتكم» is a threat: the video says so with Al-Muyassar's «وهذا تهديد شديد لهم». «مثقال ذرة» (Quran wording) is cut. STAGING v4: Madyan's town by day: Shu'ayb a blue drop labelled Shu'ayb (no plate on his name, no close-up or pan on his drop), his people three faceless men in dark robes. His clan is not drawn (the tafsirs place them nowhere in the scene). c1 (90): Shu'ayb tells them to seek forgiveness (90:1); the command is not acted by them (no raised hands, no bowing), only the camera on them (90:4); geometric for my Lord is Merciful, Loving (90:6-9, not a light plate on His attributes). c2 (91-92): they answer (91:1), shake their heads (91:4, As-Sa'di: they were weary of his advice) and point at him for we see you weak among us (91:9); the threat of stoning (91:12-14) is a counterfactual: no gesture, no stone, only the camera on them; Shu'ayb answers (92:1), the camera on them for is my clan dearer to you than Allah (92:4); nobody turns their back on 92:8-10 (a figure of speech); geometric for my Lord encompasses what you do (92:11-15). c3 (93): his last warning: Shu'ayb speaks (93:1, 93:16), the camera on them for the threat (93:4, 93:10, 93:18; Al-Muyassar: a severe threat); an hourglass for you will come to know (93:7-19); nothing of the punishment is drawn here. Cover: Shu'ayb answering them about his clan."
